# 1️⃣9️⃣ LOCAL MINIMUM

Imagine the loss surface:

```text
Loss
 ↑
 │      \       /
 │       \     /
 │        \___/
 │
 └────────────────→ parameter
```

The lowest point is a minimum.

For simple convex problems, gradient descent can converge toward the global minimum.

But deep neural networks have much more complicated loss landscapes:

```text
      __      _
 ___ /  \____/ \__
    \            /
     \__      __/
        \____/
```

There can be:

* local minima
* saddle points
* flat regions

This is one reason optimization becomes more complicated in deep learning.

