# 2️⃣0️⃣ GRADIENT DESCENT VARIANTS

You'll encounter three major types.

### Batch Gradient Descent

Uses the entire dataset for each update.

```text
All training data
      ↓
Gradient
      ↓
Update
```

Stable but potentially expensive.

---

### Stochastic Gradient Descent

Uses one sample at a time.

```text
One sample
    ↓
Gradient
    ↓
Update
```

Faster updates but noisier.

---

### Mini-Batch Gradient Descent ⭐

Uses a small batch.

Example:

```text
Dataset = 10,000 samples

Batch = 32
```

```text
32 samples
   ↓
Gradient
   ↓
Update
```

Modern deep-learning training commonly uses mini-batches.

